  "behavior": [
    "Each admitted EVM WalletConnect request receives an internal UUID, independent of the dApp session topic and reusable JSON-RPC request ID. Different live requests in one session coexist; duplicate live (topic,id) is rejected.",
    "Payloads are deep-copied on admission and publication. The queue is registered before publication; resolvers remain private. Completion is one-shot and can remove only its captured request.",
    "Approval claims one request until completion; concurrent approval or rejection cannot execute it twice. A failed broadcast consumes the intent because a transport failure may follow an accepted transaction.",
    "Popup approval and rejection carry the captured internal approval ID. Same-tick stale DOM clicks, late failures, empty queues and replacement requests cannot redirect an action to another intent.",
    "Request detail and signer derive from method-defined parameter positions, including an address-shaped personal_sign message. Object typed data serializes without throwing. The child follows replacements and the parent remounts it at a new request identity.",
    "Pending actions disable both buttons and the close action. Retry feedback is visible for the same request; a late error is not attached to the next request. Existing large button size provides at least 48-pixel height.",
    "Full WalletConnect request console logging in the extension store is removed."
  ],
